**How to implement.** The triclinic crystal builder moves onto its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16; the S10.1 brief 'TriclinicParameters gets BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `MuellerInverse.fs`, `TriclinicParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:TriclinicParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is `buildTriclinic`'s (`BiaxialSample.fs:buildTriclinic`): `{ eps = Eps.fromRefractionIndex (this.index1, this.index2, this.index3); mu = Mu.vacuum; rho = Rho.type_1_Crystal this.g11 this.g22 this.g33 this.g23 this.g13 this.g12 }`, the engine's own biaxial permittivity and full symmetric gyration tensor (`OpticalProperties/Active.fs:type_1_Crystal`). Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of a triclinic (class 1) gyrotropic crystal with these nine constants (spec 0050 §3.16). (2) Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs MUST retain buildTriclinic with its concrete parameter and return signature; its body MUST become a call to p.opticalProperties. Only the tensor-construction expression moves to the product member; the ground-truth/design builder itself MUST remain in this module and move with it to BerremanTestSupport in step 345, as 001 §Q requires. The old tensor body MUST be deleted in this step, leaving one implementation of the arithmetic. Its short contract comment MUST describe the builder without claiming a product destination. (3) BiaxialInverseTests and FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests MUST continue calling buildTriclinic for their forward models and direct tensor assertions; no test is deleted, no expected value or tolerance changes, and no product project references test support.  BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member evaluates the same record expression. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s, 5 facts) is the cheapest class whose facts drive the member through `forward`; `BiaxialInverseTests` (997 s) is not selected, as the S10.1 brief directs.

**Acceptance.** After extracting shared tensor construction, TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties MUST hold the single kernel and BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic MUST remain a test-side caller of that kernel, preserving every forward-model result and its required move to BerremanTestSupport; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.
